\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The measured system. Band-limited noise $\bm  {n}$ is added to the klystron drive after the controller; the controller output $\bm  {x}$ (TOTAL) is recorded. The beam couples to the four cavities through its dipole motion $\Delta \phi $ [Eq.~\eqref  {eq:beam}]; the klystron responds differently to drive amplitude and phase [Eq.~\eqref  {eq:klystron}]. Bold symbols are two-quadrature vectors and matrices in the cavity frame.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:loop}{{1}{2}{The measured system. Band-limited noise $\vect n$ is added to the klystron drive after the controller; the controller output $\vect x$ (TOTAL) is recorded. The beam couples to the four cavities through its dipole motion $\Delta \phi $ [Eq.~\eqref {eq:beam}]; the klystron responds differently to drive amplitude and phase [Eq.~\eqref {eq:klystron}]. Bold symbols are two-quadrature vectors and matrices in the cavity frame}{figure.1}{}}
