\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Profile likelihood of the klystron's (a) amplitude compression $g_A$ and (b) AM/PM conversion $k_\mathrm  {AP}$ at the \SI {497}{mA} operating point, with both free at every operating point, for nested data sets: one record in the routine's band (\SI {15}{}--\SI {400}{kHz}), the same record with the beam band, the gain and phase scan at \SI {497}{mA}, and all records. Every other parameter is re-optimized at each point; the dotted line marks the 95\% level ($\Delta \chi ^2=3.84$). The vertical axis is linear below 10.}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ident}{{2}{6}{Profile likelihood of the klystron's (a) amplitude compression $\gA $ and (b) AM/PM conversion $\kAP $ at the \SI {497}{mA} operating point, with both free at every operating point, for nested data sets: one record in the routine's band (\SI {15}{}--\SI {400}{kHz}), the same record with the beam band, the gain and phase scan at \SI {497}{mA}, and all records. Every other parameter is re-optimized at each point; the dotted line marks the 95\% level ($\Delta \chi ^2=3.84$). The vertical axis is linear below 10}{figure.2}{}}
